## 2026-08-23 - Searchable dropdown conversion (shared components batch)
- **Similar components found:** `src/components/ui/select.tsx` (shadcn primitive, left alone),
  `src/components/ui/transaction/SearchableSelect.tsx` (now a re-export of the canonical one),
  `react-select` in `CompanySelection.tsx` (already searchable, but non-canonical).
- **Pattern used:** MUI Autocomplete via the canonical `SearchableSelect`/`SearchableMultiSelect`
  with `variant="outlined"` as the drop-in for `FormControl` + `InputLabel` + `Select`.
- **Theme tokens used:** none added. CompanySelection now inherits colour (`color: "inherit"`,
  `borderColor: "currentColor"`) instead of the hardcoded `#005580`/white react-select styles.
- **Export pattern:** named exports for feature components (`AssignmentDropdown`,
  `CompanySelection`), default export + named type exports for `FormFieldWrapper` and `MuiSelect`.
  No barrel file in `src/components/ui/`, so nothing to update.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `FormControl` from `@/components/ui/form` is a Radix `Slot`: it forwards a
  ref to its child. A plain function component like `SearchableSelect` cannot take one, so the
  select branch of `FormFieldWrapper` renders OUTSIDE `FormControl` and an inner `SelectField`
  reads `formItemId`/`error` from `useFormField()` instead. Reuse this shape for any future
  non-forwardRef control inside a shadcn form.
- **[REUSE]** `MuiSelect` is now a thin primitive-id <-> option-object adapter over
  `SearchableSelect`. Any page still doing `options.find(...)` by hand around a raw MUI Select can
  drop straight onto `MuiSelect`.
- **Gotcha found:** the canonical `SearchableSelect` typed its Autocomplete as
  `Autocomplete<TOption, false, false, false>` while passing `disableClearable={!clearable}`
  (a `boolean`) — TS2322, repo-wide `tsc` failure. Fixed by widening the third type parameter to
  `boolean`. Check that param whenever `disableClearable` is dynamic.
- **What should change:** `FormFieldWrapper` still types `control: Control<any>` and `name: string`
  (pre-existing `any` violation). Making it generic over `TFieldValues` would require re-checking
  all 8 ctrldesk/admin consumers; worth a dedicated pass.
- **Tooling note:** `npx eslint` crashes in this repo ("Converting circular structure to JSON" from
  @eslint/eslintrc) and `next lint` has no `--file`. Use `node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit -p
  tsconfig.json` as the gate.

## 2026-08-23 - SearchableSelect rollout (accounting + BomCosting)
- **Similar components found:** src/components/ui/SearchableSelect.tsx (canonical, pre-existing); FormFieldWrapper.tsx / muiSelect.tsx / select.tsx owned by another agent this run
- **Pattern used:** MUI Autocomplete wrapper (SearchableSelect) — `variant="outlined"` for form fields, `variant="bare"` for grid/table cells
- **Theme tokens used:** none needed (component owns its styling; pages kept existing Tailwind classes)
- **Export pattern:** named export `SearchableSelect` / `SearchableMultiSelect`, no barrel file in src/components/ui
- **[REUSE]** Every raw MUI `Select`+`MenuItem` and `TextField select` in these pages was replaceable 1:1 — the only per-site work is option-object <-> id mapping and moving `error`/`helperText` off `FormControl`
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** react-hook-form `Controller` wiring moves from `{...field}` spread to explicit `value`/`onChange` + `textFieldProps={{ name, onBlur, inputRef: field.ref }}`; the `<MenuItem value="">None</MenuItem>` sentinel is replaced by `clearable` (clear = None)
- **What should change:** SearchableSelectProps has no top-level `name`/`onBlur`/`inputRef` — every RHF call site repeats the same `textFieldProps` block. A `field`-shaped convenience prop (or an RHF-aware `SearchableSelectField`) would remove that boilerplate. Also note the props type takes `TOption[]`, so `ReadonlyArray`/`Object.freeze()` option constants need a `[...spread]` at the call site; accepting `readonly TOption[]` would be better.
## 2026-08-23 - SearchableSelect rollout (dashboardadmin + dashboardctrldesk)
- **Similar components found:** `src/components/ui/FormFieldWrapper.tsx` (converted concurrently by another agent) and the page-local `dashboardadmin/userManagement/CreateUser/ControlledFormFieldWrapper.tsx` are near-duplicates of each other — same props (name/control/label/type/options/customInput), same render tree. Only difference: ControlledFormFieldWrapper adds `value` / `onChange` overrides.
- **Pattern used:** MUI Autocomplete via the shared `SearchableSelect` / `SearchableMultiSelect`, `variant="outlined"` for every labelled form field.
- **Theme tokens used:** none needed — no colors were written; MUI theme supplies the outlined field styling.
- **Export pattern:** named exports (`SearchableSelect`, `SearchableMultiSelect`) from `@/components/ui/SearchableSelect`. No barrel file in `src/components/ui/`, so imports are per-file.
- **[REUSE]** `ControlledFormFieldWrapper` should be deleted and its call sites pointed at `FormFieldWrapper` once the extra `value`/`onChange` overrides are added there (or dropped). Two copies of the same wrapper means every dropdown rule has to be applied twice — as it was here.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** shadcn `<FormControl>` is a Radix `Slot`: it forwards a ref to its child, so a plain function component (SearchableSelect) cannot be its direct child. Two working shapes: (a) render the select OUTSIDE `FormControl` in a small subcomponent that reads `useFormField()` for `formItemId` / error state (used by FormFieldWrapper and now ControlledFormFieldWrapper); (b) wrap in a `<div>` when the select must stay inside `FormControl` (used for `customInput` in orgForm).
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** Preserve exact old behaviour with `clearable={false}` — MUI `Select`/shadcn `Select` had no clear button, so the only user-visible change stays "you can now type to filter".
- **What should change:** next run, check for an already-converted sibling wrapper before touching a page — several pages (orgForm's Country/Status) needed zero edits because they route through `FormFieldWrapper`. Also: when a form prop is typed `any[]`, tighten it to a local option interface instead of letting the generic infer `any`; callers passing `any[]` still compile.

## 2026-08-23 - SearchableSelect rollout (jutePurchase + masters slice)
- **Similar components found:** `src/components/ui/transaction/SearchableSelect.tsx` is now a deprecated re-export of the canonical `@/components/ui/SearchableSelect` — no duplicate exists.
- **Pattern used:** MUI Autocomplete via canonical `SearchableSelect`; `variant="outlined"` for form fields, `variant="bare"` (default) inside line-item grids.
- **Theme tokens used:** none needed; replaced two hardcoded hexes (`#c00`/`#999` renderValue in BulkItemGrid) with the `error` prop + placeholder.
- **Export pattern:** named export from `@/components/ui/SearchableSelect` (no barrel in `src/components/ui/`).
- **[REUSE]** `SearchableSelect` replaced every `FormControl`+`InputLabel`+`Select`+`MenuItem` block in the 12 assigned files; the trio import can be dropped entirely from most pages.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `SearchableSelect` defaults to `size="small"`; pass `size="medium"` when neighbouring `TextField`s are default-size, or the field looks short.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `SearchableSelect` is a plain function component (no forwardRef), so it cannot be a direct MUI `<Tooltip>` child — wrap it in a `<Box>`.
- **What should change:** consider a `forwardRef` on `SearchableSelect` so Tooltip/Popper children work without a wrapper element.

## 2026-08-23 - SearchableOptionSelect (dropdown autofill sweep: sales/procurement + whole-tree second pass)
- **Similar components found:** `SearchableSelect` / `SearchableMultiSelect` (canonical, option-object API);
  `muiSelect.tsx`, `FormFieldWrapper.tsx`, `select.tsx` (owned by other agents this run).
- **Pattern used:** MUI (thin wrapper over the canonical `SearchableSelect` Autocomplete).
- **Why a new component:** the tree held 128 `<TextField select>` call sites that keep a *primitive*
  id in state and described options as `<MenuItem>` children. Repeating `options.find(...) ?? null`
  + `getOptionLabel` + `isOptionEqualToValue` at 128 sites would have been the alternative.
  `SearchableOptionSelect` owns the object<->id mapping once; `""` still means "nothing selected",
  so every converted `onChange` body kept working with only `e.target.value` -> `selectedValue`.
- **Theme tokens used:** none added — all colors come from the MUI theme via `SearchableSelect`.
- **Export pattern:** named export + default export; no barrel file exists in `src/components/ui/`.
- **[REUSE]** `SearchableOptionSelect` should be the default for any future primitive-valued dropdown;
  reach for `SearchableSelect` directly only when form state stores the whole option object.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** A placeholder `<MenuItem value="">None/All/Select…</MenuItem>` no longer exists
  as an option — it becomes `placeholder="..."` plus the Autocomplete clear (x) button, which emits `""`.
  Where clearing must be impossible, pass `clearable={false}`.
- **What should change:** `src/components/ui/` has no `index.ts`; a barrel would stop these near-duplicate
  wrappers from being rediscovered. Also, ESLint is currently unrunnable in this repo
  (`next lint` / `eslint` both crash on the flat-config: "Converting circular structure to JSON"),
  so only `tsc --noEmit` and `vitest` can gate a sweep this size.

## 2026-08-25 - Breakdown entry screen responsive pass (juteMechanical/breakdown)
- **Similar components found:** `src/components/ui/responsiveEntry.tsx` already existed and was the
  correct home for every constant needed — nothing new was declared. The house pattern in practice
  is `jutePurchase/juteIssue/edit/page.tsx` (DESKTOP_ONLY_SX table + MOBILE_ONLY_SX card list).
- **Pattern used:** MUI + CSS-only `sx` breakpoints. No `useMediaQuery`, no width check — both
  layouts render, CSS picks one, so the pages' `mounted` hydration guards stay meaningful.
- **Theme tokens used:** none added. Colors stayed on palette keys (`success`/`warning`/`error`,
  `background.paper`, `text.secondary`, `divider`, `action.hover`).
- **Export pattern:** default export per `_components/*` file (page-local), named exports from
  `@/components/ui/responsiveEntry`. Still no barrel in `src/components/ui/`.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `sx={[SHARED_SX, { ...override }]}` does NOT typecheck on MUI `Box`: the
  shared constant is typed `SxProps<Theme>` (a union that already includes the array form) and
  `Box`'s array element type rejects it (TS2769). Compose instead — here a
  `<Box sx={{ flexGrow: 1, display: { xs: "none", sm: "block" } }} />` spacer replaced the
  `justifyContent: flex-end` that STICKY_ACTIONS_SX does not carry. Reuse the spacer trick rather
  than casting.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** To turn a line-item grid row into a card only below `md`, keep ONE DOM node:
  `<Paper variant="outlined" sx={{ p: {xs:1.5, md:0}, border: {md:"none"}, bgcolor: {md:"transparent"},
  gridTemplateColumns: { xs: "repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr))", md: "<the real row>" } }}`, then span the
  wide fields with `gridColumn: { xs: "1 / -1", md: "auto" }`. A breakpoint object with only an
  `md` key leaves the `xs` value coming from the MUI variant class, and sx out-specifies it.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** CSS `order` with breakpoints (`order: { xs: 3, md: 0 }`) re-sequences a
  wrapping flex row on a phone without touching DOM order, so the desktop layout is provably
  unchanged. Used on OpenBreakdownBoard to get chips / detail / full-width Close on three bands.
- **[REUSE]** `MobileCard` + `CardStat` absorbed the whole mobile branch of a 17-column DataGrid.
  Any other juteMechanical grid (overhaul, PM execution, reports) can take the same shape: pick the
  4 fields that identify the record, leave the rest on the desktop grid.
- **Gotcha:** `SearchableOptionSelect` is a plain function component, so grid placement (`gridColumn`)
  belongs on a wrapping `<Box>`, not on the select itself.
- **What should change:** `responsiveEntry.tsx` has no `MOBILE_CARD_ROW_SX` for the
  "grid row below md, card above" line-item case — the Paper sx above was hand-written twice in this
  module. Lifting it would be the next useful addition. Gate stays `npx tsc --noEmit` +
  `npx vitest run --project unit` (ESLint is still unrunnable in this repo).

## 2026-08-25 - juteMechanical overhaul + preventiveMaintenance mobile pass (360px)
- **Similar components found:** none new. `src/components/ui/responsiveEntry.tsx` (the shared kit) had ZERO consumers before this run — the only prior implementation was the page-local `DESKTOP_ONLY_SX` const inlined at `jutePurchase/juteIssue/edit/page.tsx:114`.
- **Pattern used:** MUI, CSS-only breakpoints via `sx`. DataGrid wrapped in `DESKTOP_ONLY_SX` with a parallel `MOBILE_ONLY_SX` card list fed from the SAME rows prop; no `useMediaQuery` anywhere (these pages have `mounted` hydration guards that a JS width check would defeat).
- **Theme tokens used:** none added. Colors come from the MUI palette (`error.main` via `alpha()`, `divider`, `background.paper`, Chip `color` props).
- **Export pattern:** named exports from `@/components/ui/responsiveEntry` (no barrel in `src/components/ui/`).
- **[REUSE]** `jutePurchase/juteIssue/edit/page.tsx` still declares its own local `DESKTOP_ONLY_SX`; it should import the shared one and delete the local const.
- **[REUSE]** The mobile pager (Prev / "n / m" / Next driving the same server-side `page` state) had to be hand-rolled in BOTH `OverhaulGrid` and `PmExecutionGrid` — the DataGrid footer lives inside the grid and so vanishes with it below `md`. This is now duplicated twice and will be duplicated again by every grid that gets this treatment. It belongs in `responsiveEntry.tsx` as a `MobilePager` component.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `STICKY_ACTIONS_SX` does not set `justifyContent`, and spreading an `SxProps<Theme>` union does not typecheck. Merge extra layout via Box SYSTEM PROPS instead: `<Box sx={STICKY_ACTIONS_SX} justifyContent={{ xs: "stretch", sm: "flex-end" }}>`. sx wins over system props, and since the constant omits the key there is no conflict.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `STICKY_ACTIONS_SX` already sizes its children via `& .MuiButton-root` (flex + minHeight), so per-button `sx={{ minHeight: 44, width: {xs:"100%"} }}` must be dropped or it fights the container. Use the exported `TOUCH_TARGET` rather than a literal 44.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** For a small FIXED enum (<= 3 codes) on a phone, a `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive, fullWidth, `& .MuiToggleButton-root { minHeight: TOUCH_TARGET, flex: 1 }`) beats any dropdown for one-handed use. It is NOT a dropdown, so it does not violate the searchable-dropdown rule — but gate it on `options.length <= 3` and fall back to `SearchableSelect variant="outlined" size="medium"` when the server returns more codes, so a longer enum never degrades into unreachable segments.
- **What should change:** `MobileCard` was not usable in the grid cards here — its children slot is hardcoded to a 2-column `CardStat` grid, so a card needing a wrapped free-text tail (work_done / remarks) below the stats has to hand-roll the Paper. Give `MobileCard` a `footer` slot, or let the caller opt out of the built-in grid.
